Still failing — ld.lld segfaults during the final libarm64ecfex.dll link.
Attempted workarounds in this commit:

1. --whole-archive on libc++ + libc++abi to force EC-mangled symbol resolution
   (resolved: __libcpp_verbose_abort, __wide_to_char)
2. Added IOSStubs.S to provide non-EC-mangled aliases for symbols that libc++abi
   only defines as EC-mangled but the linker references as plain (access, btowc,
   wctob, __gxx_personality_seh0)
3. Mixed -lmsvcrt -lkernel32 -lucrt for stripped runtime support

Last known error after all these: ld.lld segfault on link. Suspect llvm-mingw
22.1.4's arm64ec C++ runtime support isn't mature enough — EC-mangling is
inconsistent between the C++ compiler frontend's references and what's defined
in the C++ stdlib archives.

Resume strategies for next session:
- try newer llvm-mingw release (22.x → 23.x?)
- try Linux-host arm64ec cross-compile chain (proper MSVC-aligned EC support)
- disable LTO globally + clean rebuild (LTO + arm64ec interaction may segfault)
- consider pivoting back to WoW64 for first-game milestone, since that path's
  C runtime support is cleaner and the same iOS x18 strategy applies

The x18 substitution work in the prior commit is reusable for any of these.

